  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Dilaudid (hydromorphone immediate release) Criteria Version 2. Original 6/13/2007; Approval 11/15/2019; Effective 1/6/2020.",
    "Formulations: tablets 2/4/8 mg; oral solution 1 mg/mL; suppositories 3 mg.",
    "Indicated for pain severe enough to require an opioid analgesic when alternative treatments are inadequate. Reserve for patients whose alternatives (non-opioid analgesics or physical therapy) are not tolerated or cannot achieve adequate analgesia.",
    "Pharmacy hospice/cancer/LTC override waives standard approval criteria; the closed moderate-to-severe pain indication and both safety denial gates apply on both paths.",
    "Standard regimen branches: single agent requires hydromorphone IR ≤24 mg/day; concurrent long-acting opioid requires the State Alaska Drug Utilization Committee average daily morphine equivalent dose limit and PRN breakthrough dosing. Dose compliance is attested; the source does not state a numeric MME ceiling.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor addiction, abuse and misuse; serious, life-threatening or fatal respiratory depression may occur. Benzodiazepines or other CNS depressants, including alcohol, may cause profound sedation, respiratory depression, coma and death.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months if positive clinical improvement. Quantity limit (notes only): up to 30-day supply. Duration, renewal and quantity enforcement remain manual review.",
    "References: Hydromorphone package insert, Halo Pharmaceutical, December 2016 (accessed October 16, 2019); CDC Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Chronic Pain — United States, 2016, MMWR 65(1):1–49, March 18, 2016."
  ],
